  <title>Overview</title>
  <updated>2026-11-10T00:00:00.000Z</updated>
  <author><name>DocKitty Example</name></author>
  <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://spec-kitty.github.io/doc-kitty/architecture/overview/"/>
  <summary>How the example turns a Common Docs tree into a site plus feeds and an agent-API.</summary>
  <content type="html">&lt;span id=&quot;overview&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The site is a static Astro + Starlight build driven entirely by the &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;docs/&lt;/code&gt;
tree.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;figure class=&quot;dk-diagram&quot; role=&quot;group&quot; aria-labelledby=&quot;dk-diagram-caption-0&quot;&gt;&lt;pre class=&quot;mermaid&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;flowchart LR
accTitle: Build pipeline
accDescr: The docs/ tree feeds the toolkit loader, which fans out to Starlight, the sitemap, RSS, llms.txt, and the agent-API, then Starlight emits the static site.
  D[docs/**  README-as-index + frontmatter] --&gt; L[toolkit loader]
  L --&gt; S[Starlight  nav / search / theme]
  L --&gt; M[sitemap-index.xml]
  L --&gt; R[rss.xml]
  L --&gt; T[llms.txt]
  L --&gt; A[&quot;/api/*.json  agent-API&quot;]
  S --&gt; H[dist/  static HTML]&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;figcaption class=&quot;dk-diagram__caption&quot; id=&quot;dk-diagram-caption-0&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;dk-diagram__desc&quot;&gt;The docs/ tree feeds the toolkit loader, which fans out to Starlight, the sitemap, RSS, llms.txt, and the agent-API, then Starlight emits the static site.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;page-metadata-model&quot;&gt;Page metadata model&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every page carries the same frontmatter, and its section comes from the
section registry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;figure class=&quot;dk-diagram&quot; role=&quot;group&quot; aria-labelledby=&quot;dk-diagram-caption-1&quot;&gt;&lt;pre class=&quot;mermaid&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;erDiagram
accTitle: Page metadata model
accDescr: A section holds many pages; each page carries one frontmatter block and may relate to other pages.
  SECTION ||--o{ PAGE : holds
  PAGE ||--|| FRONTMATTER : carries
  PAGE }o--o{ PAGE : relates_to
  FRONTMATTER {
    string title
    string description
    string doc_status
    datetime updated
    string kind
  }&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;figcaption class=&quot;dk-diagram__caption&quot; id=&quot;dk-diagram-caption-1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;dk-diagram__desc&quot;&gt;A section holds many pages; each page carries one frontmatter block and may relate to other pages.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;key-properties&quot;&gt;Key properties&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Static&lt;/strong&gt; — no server; everything renders at build time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Metadata-driven&lt;/strong&gt; — nav, feeds, and the agent-API all read from frontmatter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Convention-first&lt;/strong&gt; — the &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;docs/&lt;/code&gt; tree is a valid OKF bundle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See the toolkit’s own architecture docs for the internals.&lt;/p&gt;</content>
